Description: Eject removable drives through UDisks2 instead of the umount binary
 umount needs privileges the sandbox does not have. Calling
 org.freedesktop.UDisks2.Filesystem.Unmount works unprivileged and lets
 the desktop show its safe-removal notification. Makes the bundled
 umount shim redundant.
 The device node is resolved through any symlink and encoded the way
 UDisks2 names its block device objects, keeping alphanumeric characters
 and writing every other byte as an underscore and two hex digits, so an
 encrypted drive at /dev/mapper/luks-<uuid> reaches the object dm_2d0.
 A drive that answers DeviceBusy is tried again a few times, since the
 eject button is pressed right after an export, when the file may still be
 held open for a moment by something outside the application.
